{"name": "Aetosaurus", "clade": "aetosaurinae", "isd": false, "isnote": "", "sum": "Aetosaurus is an extinct pseudosuchian aetosaur of the Late Triassic of Europe, Greenland and North America, generally regarded as the most primitive aetosaur.", "wsnote": "No length or mass estimate is given in the sources consulted.", "holotype": "Not stated in the sources consulted for this draft; A. ferratus was named by Fraas in 1877.", "material": "Many specimens from the Norian of Germany, Switzerland, Italy and Greenland, including slabs with several individuals; additional remains referred from the Chinle Group of the south-western United States.", "completeness": "multiple", "exceptional": "", "biology": "Its long, narrow carapace lacked the lateral spikes of more derived aetosaurs such as Desmatosuchus; a slab with many individuals has been discussed as possible evidence of gregarious behaviour.", "author": "Fraas 1877", "fad": 227.3, "lad": 205.7, "early": "Norian", "late": "", "type_species": "Aetosaurus ferratus", "pbdb_occ": 6, "species": [{"name": "Aetosaurus crassicauda", "author": "Fraas 1907", "fad": 227.3, "lad": 205.7, "interval": "Norian", "ref": ""}, {"name": "Aetosaurus ferratus", "author": "Fraas 1877", "fad": 227.3, "lad": 205.7, "interval": "Norian", "ref": "original description"}], "formations": [{"ids": ["lowenstein-germany"], "formation": "Löwenstein", "group": "Keuper", "members": ["Lower Stubensandstein"], "country": "Germany", "regions": ["Baden-Württemberg", "Baden-Württenburg"], "interval": "Norian", "n": 3, "ma": [205.7, 227.3]}, {"ids": ["klettgau-switzerland"], "formation": "Klettgau", "group": "Keuper", "members": ["Gruhalde"], "country": "Switzerland", "regions": ["Aargau"], "interval": "Norian", "n": 1, "ma": [205.7, 227.3]}, {"ids": ["fleming-fjord-greenland"], "formation": "Ørsted Dal", "group": "Fleming Fjord", "members": [], "country": "Greenland", "regions": [], "interval": "Norian", "n": 1, "ma": [205.7, 227.3]}, {"ids": ["zorzino-limest